## Docker

A macOS app cannot run in a Linux container: the window, the Rust build and the `.app`/`.dmg` are always made on this Mac. The Docker image is a Linux toolchain (Node.js and Rust); `node_modules` and Rust builds of the containers stay in Docker volumes.
{% if choices.docker == "full" %}
The npm dependencies, the Vite dev server, all checks and tests, and the web build run in the `dev` container:

```sh
docker compose run --rm dev npm install      # after cloning or changing dependencies
npm run dev                                  # starts the dev container and opens the window
docker compose run --rm dev npm run check    # any npm script
npm run build                                # .app and .dmg (the web build runs in the container)
docker compose down --volumes --rmi local    # delete the containers, volumes and image
```
{% else %}
Development and builds run on this Mac. The `check` service runs the quality gate from a clean install in a Linux container, like CI:

```sh
docker compose run --rm --build check        # npm ci + npm run check
docker compose down --volumes --rmi local    # delete the volumes and the image
```
{% endif %}{% endif %}
